====================
Tokens
====================

NUMBER		-> [0-9]+
NEW_LINE	-> "\n"
DIVIDER		-> "=" "=" "=" "=" "=" "=" "=" "=" "=" "="
SPACE		-> " "
COLON		-> ":"
EOF			-> "\0"
STRING		-> Everything else

====================
Grammar
====================

log_file		-> log+ EOF
log				-> date elapsed_time log_msg log_divider
date			-> (STRING | SPACE | NUMBER | COLON)+ NEW_LINE
elapsed_time	-> (STRING | SPACE)+ COLON SPACE NUMBER NEW_LINE
log_msg			-> (STRING | SPACE | NUMBER | COLON | NEW_LINE)* NEW_LINE
log_divider		-> DIVIDER NEW_LINE


Reserved keywords:
DIVIDER is a reserved keyword. It can't be a part of the log_msg in a log file.
Might be a good idea to check for reserved keywords before commiting log
message to the log file when executing the "stop" command.


